Here's the updated code with ARIA wiring so the invalid state is exposed to assistive technology (via `aria-invalid` on the fieldset and `aria-describedby` linking it to the error message):

```js
updated(changedProperties) {
  if (changedProperties.has('error') || changedProperties.has('validity')) {
    const invalid = this.validity && this.validity !== 'valid';

    // existing behaviour: mirror the error attribute onto each child
    this.items.forEach((el) => {
      if (this.error) el.setAttribute('error', '');
      else el.removeAttribute('error');

      if (invalid) el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
      else el.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
    });
  }
}

render() {
  const invalid = this.validity && this.validity !== 'valid';

  return html`
    <fieldset
      role="radiogroup"
      aria-invalid=${invalid ? 'true' : 'false'}
      aria-describedby=${this.error ? 'group-error' : nothing}
    >
      <legend><slot name="legend"></slot></legend>
      <slot></slot>
      ${this.error
        ? html`<p id="group-error" role="alert" aria-live="assertive">${this.error}</p>`
        : nothing}
    </fieldset>
  `;
}
```

Key changes:
- `aria-invalid` on the `fieldset` reflects `validity !== 'valid'` (covers both `valueMissing` and `customError`, not just when `error` text is present).
- `aria-describedby="group-error"` on the fieldset ties the group to the error `<p>` persistently, so AT that doesn't catch the live-region announcement (e.g. a screen reader landing on the group later) still discovers the error text.
- `updated()` now also triggers on `validity` changes (not just `error`), and mirrors `aria-invalid` onto each radio item so per-item state is exposed too.
